WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is now --
We're a few weeks after

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:04.170
he signed the order
to stop the family separations.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
They gave themselves
a deadline of this Thursday

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:08.341 line:92%
to reunite all the families.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where are we at right now
in that?

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.411
-So let's talk about this.
There, today, right now,

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:14.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
as we sit here,
2,551 kids were ripped away

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
from their parents
by the Trump administration,

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we should keep saying
over and over again,

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
till every one of these kids
is accounted for,

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this is not something
that had ever happened before.

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a policy
that was put into place

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:27.594
to systematically take these
kids away from their parents.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:30.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a crisis on the scale
of a natural disaster

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was manmade
by the Trump administration.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:35.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a crisis
of their own creation.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.436 line:92%
Thursday is the deadline.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're now saying
that something like 900

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:41.875 line:92%
of the 2,551 have been reunited,

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:42.609 size:84% position:42% line:92%
but they're also saying

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:46.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
over a third
may never, ever be reunited,

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
or, at least,
it's gonna be very complicated

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
to put these people
back together.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:50.784 line:92%
And we just have to continue

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:51.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
to demand answers
from the administration,

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.920
because none of these kids
should have been separated

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:54.587 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in the first place.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:57.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, that failure
to reunite the children,

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:59.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
is this a byproduct
of how terribly planned

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
this was to begin with?
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.129 size:84% position:42% line:92%
There was never a plan.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
First of all, some of
the shelters that I went to --

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I went inside
some of these places --

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was the most
harrowing experience

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:11.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a father of a young kid,
like you,

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.238 line:92%
that I've ever seen in my life.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:15.308
The shelters, for the most part,
take good care of the kids.

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.310 size:84% position:42%
But they didn't know
these kids were coming,

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.778 line:92%
separated from their parents.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:21.848
The thing that disgusts me,
and I will never forget,

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:24.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that they took these kids
away from their parents

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:24.717 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and put them in cages.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was one of
the small group of journalists

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:29.756
that got to go inside the
border patrol processing station

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
in McAllen, Texas,
and see these little kids

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
sitting around
under a watch tower,

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
playing by themselves,
because of the idea

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Donald Trump thought it
would scare other people

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:41.134 line:92%
from coming into this country.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now,
because there was no plan

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:43.903 line:92%
to ever put it back together,

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:46.673
you could have kids that their
parents were already deported,

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:48.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they may never
see them again.

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.710 line:92%
-There's this sense now that,

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
they're trying to fix it.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think
they're trying to fix it

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.048 size:78% position:39% line:92%
because they realized

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:58.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
how awful an act it was
in the first place,

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
or do you think
they're just trying to fix

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:00.920 line:92%
what has become a PR disaster?

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
And I'll tell you something.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:03.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw Sean Spicer
in this building.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I'm sorry.
-Yeah, exactly. Thank you.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:06.793 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:09.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw him in the building
the other day.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:10.530 line:92%
And he was -- I asked him.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said,
"What'd you think about it?"

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.800 line:92%
And he said, "It was a mess."

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.667 line:92%
And he was saying it was a mess

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
just like the Muslim ban
was a mess.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because it wasn't
well-thought-through.

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:20.406 line:92%
Not because this was inhumane

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
to take kids away
from their parents,

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
not because --
and that's the same thing

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:24.577 line:92%
with putting them back together.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not because
we feel bad about it

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.915
but because we just kind of
messed up and it looked bad.

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:29.916 line:92%
And the President admitted that.

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
When we were down there,
from day one,

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
when we were in the shelter
in Brownsville,

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:34.654 line:92%
to day seven, I think it was,

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:37.190
that he signed the executive
order to put them back together,

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:39.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
he basically said,
"I saw you guys on TV.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw the writing,
I saw the pictures,

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:43.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's sort of
why we did this.

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:45.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
It didn't look that good."
-Yeah.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:47.200 line:92%
You're doing incredible work.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for continuing it.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's obviously very exciting
for me to see you

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.072
because I've been following
the work you're doing on TV.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:54.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
Other people
are excited to see you

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:55.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they think
you're someone else.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:57.076 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, that's true.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
J.J. Abrams.
-J.J. Abrams.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:02:59.812 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here, why don't you
hold that up for us.

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:03.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I will say --
-Yeah, go right over there.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm not, uh...
-Yeah.

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:07.387 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I'm not nearly as rich.

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:08.254 line:92%
In fact, I'm not anywhere close.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.956 size:84% position:42%
"I would love to have
the J.J. Abrams money,"

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.358
is what I say to when people
come up to me on the street.

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:13.693 size:75% position:38% line:92%
So, J.J., hit me up.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:14.460 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, there you go.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, thank you very much
for being here.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:16.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can I have this?
-Yeah, you can have that.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's the least we can do.
-Thank you very much.

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:19.098 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Okay, thank you.

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, thanks for being here,
Jacob.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.236 size:84% position:42%
Keep up the great work.
I really appreciate it.

